  "scenario": {
    "id": "QA-D1-CANARY-TWO-TURN",
    "title": "hourly canary: PDF mention + mentioned follow-up in one thread, file persists",
    "friction": [
      "D1",
      "D22",
      "D7",
      "F4",
      "F15",
      "I7",
      "NEW-1"
    ],
    "set": "A",
    "surface": "discord",
    "tier": "canary",
    "priority": "P0",
    "est_turns": 2,
    "notes": "Catches at once: D1 session replaced on follow-up (log + latency + preamble), stuck Working-on-it card (D6), channel-level Opening/Your chat is ready (D20), silent drop of a mention with a PDF attachment (NEW-1 / no-reply 10-09), slow first output (D16), (empty response) (I3), and lost working files (D7/F1 shape: write in turn 1, read in turn 2). The file value is random and never shown in chat, so turn 2 can only print it by reading the file. Prod: run in the dedicated canary channel of the internal guild (runner config), not a new channel.",
    "setup": [],
    "steps": [
      {
        "do": "new_channel"
      },
      {
        "do": "mention",
        "file": "fixtures/canary.pdf",
        "text": "QA canary, turn 1. Do exactly this: (1) read the attached PDF; (2) run this bash command in your working directory and do not show its output: python3 -c \"import secrets;print(secrets.token_hex(6))\" > qa_canary.txt ; (3) reply with only one line: CODE=<the code word printed in the PDF>"
      },
      {
        "do": "wait_done",
        "timeout_s": 180
      },
      {
        "do": "thread_reply",
        "mention": true,
        "text": "QA canary, turn 2. Run `cat qa_canary.txt` in your working directory and reply with only one line: FILE=<its exact contents>, or FILE=MISSING if the file does not exist."
      },
      {
        "do": "wait_done",
        "timeout_s": 180
      }
    ],
